  {
    "test_name": "Hatch Patterns::Empty boundary returns nothing",
    "bridge_function": "OCCTHatchLines",
    "bridge_output": {
      "type": "hatch",
      "data": {
        "empty_boundary_segments": 0,
        "empty_boundary_with_island_segments": 0
      }
    },
    "kernel_output": {
      "type": "hatch",
      "data": {
        "empty_boundary_segments_unguarded": 0,
        "empty_boundary_with_island_segments_unguarded": 3
      }
    },
    "kernel_probe": "Scripts/repro/766-hatch-redo/probe.mm",
    "comparison": {
      "equal": false,
      "differences": [
        "Expected divergence, and the behaviour under test: HatchPattern.generate and OCCTHatchLines both reject a boundary with fewer than 3 points before any Hatch_Hatcher call, so the island-only case returns 0 segments through the bridge. The kernel probe deliberately skips both guards (the _unguarded keys): with an empty boundary and no island it also returns 0, but with an island alone the island sets the extent and its own edges trim the lines into 3 segments (transcript.txt: 'emptyBoundary + island (unguarded kernel path): segments=3'). Bridge 0 versus unguarded kernel 3 is a value difference caused by the guard, not a key-name difference."
      ]
    },
    "status": "EXPECTED_DIVERGENCE"
  }
]
